  "reason": "With only one completed experiment (config_002: multimodal/multiprofile/scgpt/resnet50/transformer/weighted at 49.4% acc), the most critical uncertainty is whether the multimodal fusion is actually adding value over a single-modality baseline. config_001 (image_only, multiprofile, resnet50, transformer) is the cleanest ablation of config_002—it holds image encoder, profile setting, and aggregation identical, removing only the RNA branch. If image-only accuracy is close to 49.4%, RNA is not contributing and I should focus on image-side improvements; if it is substantially lower, the RNA signal is valuable and I should explore better RNA encoders and fusion strategies; if it is substantially higher, the RNA branch is hurting and I should pivot. Establishing this single-modality baseline is the highest-leverage uncertainty reduction with 8 experiments remaining, as it determines whether to invest in multimodal refinement or single-modality optimization for the rest of the budget."
}

